2:T705,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does it cost to replace a kitchen tap in the UK?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"As a rough guide, a straightforward replacement may typically cost around £120–£350, including a standard tap and labour. Premium taps and plumbing complications can increase the total. Every project differs, so request a free, no-obligation quote for accurate pricing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does a plumber charge to fit a kitchen tap?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"As a rough guide, labour may be around £80–£180 for an uncomplicated replacement, although call-out charges, local rates and the condition of the existing fittings affect the price. Obtain a free, no-obligation quote for an accurate project-specific cost."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I replace a kitchen tap without replacing the sink?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Usually, yes. The new tap must suit the existing hole pattern, sink thickness and plumbing connections. An adapter or cover plate may be needed if the arrangements differ."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why is my kitchen tap replacement quote higher than expected?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Possible reasons include seized fittings, corroded pipework, faulty isolation valves, poor access beneath the sink or the need for adapters and replacement connectors."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is it cheaper to repair or replace a kitchen tap?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A repair, such as replacing a cartridge or washer, may cost less if the tap is otherwise in good condition. Replacement may be more practical where the tap body is corroded or several parts are failing."}}]}7:["slug","how-much-does-it-cost-to-replace-a-kitchen-tap-uk","d"]
